## (7) 1440 for the record — the phone rule deliberately does not apply there
    1440x900 closed  brightest rgb(250,250,250)  L 0.9560  379/2852 over the
                     phone ceiling.
  That is the portrait at full value and the mark at opacity 0.92, which is what
  the launcher block prescribes from 87.5rem up ("the page's own gutter (96px at
  --page-max) holds the disc clear of the measure, so the face is shown at full
  value and the mark with it"). TC-MV-OCCLUDE-01/02 are phone-only by design —
  the spec hard-pins VIEWPORT to 390x844 and says so in its own header — so this
  number is a description of the desktop launcher, not a failure of it. The
  desktop suites that do run at 1440 are green: MONO-MV-01 @ 1440 and
  TC-MV-LABEL-01 @ 1440.
